# SauceDemo – Manual Testing Test Plan

## 1. Project Overview

**Project Name:** SauceDemo Manual Testing  
**Application:** SauceDemo  
**Testing Type:** Manual Testing  
**Testing Approach:** Functional Testing  
**Prepared By:** QA Tester  
**Status:** Planned

This project aims to evaluate the functionality and behavior of the SauceDemo web application through manual testing.

## 2. Test Objectives

The main objectives of this testing project are:

- Verify that users can log in using valid credentials.
- Validate product listing and product details functionality.
- Verify shopping cart operations.
- Validate product sorting functionality.
- Test checkout functionality and form validation.
- Identify and document any defects found during testing.
- Ensure that the application's main user flows work as expected.

## 3. Scope of Testing

The following features are included in the testing scope:

- User Login
- Product Listing
- Product Details
- Product Sorting
- Add to Cart
- Remove from Cart
- Shopping Cart
- Continue Shopping
- Checkout Process
- Checkout Form Validation

## 4. Out of Scope

The following areas are excluded from this testing project:

- Payment Gateway Integration
- Security and Penetration Testing
- Performance and Load Testing
- Backend and Database Testing
- Cross-Browser Compatibility Testing
- Mobile Application Testing

## 5. Testing Types

The following testing types will be performed:

- **Functional Testing:** To verify that application features work according to their expected behavior.
- **Positive Testing:** To validate the application using valid inputs and expected user actions.
- **Negative Testing:** To verify how the application handles invalid inputs and unexpected user actions.
- **UI Testing:** To check the visual elements and basic interface behavior.
- **Validation Testing:** To verify required fields and input validation messages.
- **Regression Testing:** To ensure that previously working features remain functional after changes or fixes.

## 6. Test Environment

| Component | Details |
|---|---|
| Application | SauceDemo |
| Browser | Google Chrome |
| Operating System | Windows 11 |
| Testing Type | Manual |
| Testing Environment | Web Application |
| Browser Version | Not recorded |

## 7. Entry Criteria

Testing can begin when:

- The application is accessible.
- Valid test credentials are available.
- The test environment is ready.
- Test scenarios and test cases have been prepared.

## 8. Exit Criteria

Testing will be considered complete when:

- All planned test cases have been executed.
- Test results have been documented.
- Identified defects have been reported.
- Retesting and regression testing have been completed where applicable.
- A final test summary report has been prepared.

## 9. Test Deliverables

The following deliverables will be maintained throughout the project:

- Test Plan
- Test Scenarios
- Test Cases
- Bug Reports
- Test Execution Report
- Test Summary Report
- Supporting Screenshots and Evidence

## 10. Risks and Assumptions

- Testing depends on the availability of the SauceDemo application.
- Application behavior may change over time.
- The project uses a publicly available demo application.
- Testing is limited to the features accessible through the selected test environment.

